runtime_finding rf:substrate-python-floor
  severity medium
  claim the substrate implementation requires Python 3.10 or newer; the host default python3 is 3.9.6
  mechanism planner.py calls int.bit_count(), added in Python 3.10
  observed under the default interpreter the validator raises AttributeError: 'int' object has no attribute 'bit_count'
  observed under /opt/homebrew/bin/python3.12 every check passes
  consequence a reader running the validator with the default interpreter would conclude the substrates are broken; they are not
  ladder_localization capability YES, body YES, service N/A, host runtime NO under default interpreter, YES under 3.11 or 3.12
  pattern this is the fourth admission-ladder instance this session, after the atlas MCP wrapper, the absent php body and the unhosted AppPack routes
  action record the interpreter floor as a property of the executable identity, not as a defect

